// The existential over the labels of a tracked region.
//
// exists(l, labels, psi) holds where psi holds for some label l of the image
// labels; here the labels of the lesion at frame 0, which is where tracked
// numbers its regions. It unrolls, as until does, into a disjunction over 1..K
// with l instantiated, K the bound given with --maxlabels -- the memoisation of
// the second pass then shares whatever does not depend on l. The bound is a
// hypothesis of the run: the third pass prints its check beside the program,
// and --probe computes it from the data. See exists-footprint for the same
// shape on a region that works today.
//
// l is a free identifier, as the frame reference n is; the binder is the only
// thing that tells them apart. It has to be lower case: the parser reads an
// initial capital as an operator.
//
// The goal: a voxel that is in a tracked region now and still in the same one
// at the next frame, for some region -- the lesion persists, per component.
let study = load("study.nii.gz")
let lesion = gt(intensity(frame(study,n)),500)
let region(l) = tracked(lesion,l)
save "persistent" exists(l,initially(lcc(lesion)),and(region(l),diamond(region(l))))
